{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Eviction Law criminal-conviction causes (assault, theft, drugs, human trafficking)","requirement":"A landlord may file for eviction when a tenant is convicted of, pleads guilty to, or is civilly found liable for assault or threats against the landlord, theft on the premises, drug activity, or human trafficking, or permits such a person to live there.","key_value":"3-day Notice to Quit; suit within 2 years of conviction, release or delinquency, whichever is later","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies; the specific causes stated in the Eviction Law at N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1","quoted_span":"A Notice to Quit must be served on the tenant at least three days prior to filing suit for eviction (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1(q)).","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Owner-occupied two- and three-family dwelling evictions","requirement":"Tenants of a landlord-occupied two- or three-family dwelling may be removed only by court order for listed causes, with a three-month notice for at-will or year-to-year tenancies, one month for month-to-month, and three-day notice for disorderly, destructive or rule-violating causes.","key_value":"3-month notice (at-will/year-to-year); 1-month (month-to-month); 3-day (disorderly/destructive/rule violations)","coverage_conditions":"Owner-occupied two- and three-family dwellings.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"covered","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":3}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["Tenants of landlord-occupied two- and three-family dwellings can be removed only when a court issues an order for eviction."]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.2","quoted_span":"Tenants of landlord-occupied two- and three-family dwellings can be removed only when a court issues an order for eviction.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Rooming and boarding house eviction causes and notice","requirement":"Owners of rooming and boarding houses must follow the good causes and notice requirements of the Eviction Law when evicting residents, and must give the County Welfare Board at least three working days' notice before starting an eviction action.","key_value":"3 working days' notice to County Welfare Board","coverage_conditions":"Buildings with at least two living units occupied by unrelated persons without private kitchens and bathrooms, unless one of the Rooming and Boarding House Act exceptions applies.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"other","role":"covered","text":"Rooming and boarding houses: at least two living units occupied by unrelated persons without private kitchens and bathrooms"}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["Any building having at least two (2) living units occupied by persons unrelated to each other"]},"exemptions":"Hotels with more than 85 percent temporary occupancy by people with homes elsewhere; school and college dormitories; buildings housing only college students; and certain residences for the disabled.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.A.C. 5:27-3.3","quoted_span":"require owners of rooming and boarding houses to follow the good causes and notice requirements of the Eviction Law when evicting residents, except if otherwise ordered by the Bureau (N.J.A.C. 5:27-3.3(c)).","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Penalties for eviction law violations (owner-occupancy and demolition)","requirement":"A landlord who evicts a tenant to personally occupy the unit must occupy it at least six months, and a landlord who evicts to permanently board up, demolish or retire a unit from residential use may not use the property residentially for five years.","key_value":"6 months' owner occupancy; 5-year residential-use bar; up to $10,000 civil penalty per violation","coverage_conditions":"All residential rentals; applies to landlords who obtained eviction for owner occupancy or for retiring a unit from residential use.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Three times the damages suffered plus attorney fees and costs; and, for residential use during the five-year period, a civil penalty up to $10,000.00 for each violation.","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.6","quoted_span":"When a tenant vacates a dwelling unit after having been given notice that the landlord wishes to personally occupy the unit the landlord must occupy the unit for at least six (6) months.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Reprisal against tenants exercising civil rights","requirement":"A landlord may not evict, alter a lease, or refuse to renew in reprisal against a tenant who enforces lease or legal rights, complains to a government authority, joins a tenant organization, or refuses a reprisal lease change.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All rental properties used for dwelling purposes, including mobile homes, except owner-occupied two- or three-family dwellings.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":3}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["The law against reprisal applies to all rental properties used for dwelling purposes, including mobile homes, except owner-occupied two- or three-family dwellings."]},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied two- or three-family dwellings.","penalty":"The tenant may sue the landlord for damages in a civil action.","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:42-10.10","quoted_span":"A landlord cannot take reprisal action against a tenant by eviction, substantial alteration of a lease or its terms, or refusal to renew a lease when a tenant exercises certain civil rights (N.J.S.A. 2A:42-10.10).","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Tenant protections in foreclosure","requirement":"Foreclosure alone is not grounds for eviction; a buyer wanting to personally occupy a foreclosed unit must give a 90-day notice to quit, and a new owner must notify tenants within 10 business days of the sale that they need not move.","key_value":"90-day notice to quit; tenant notice within 10 business days after sale","coverage_conditions":"Residential rental units in foreclosed properties; owner-occupied two- and three-family units are not exempt from the 90-day notice requirement.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:50-69","quoted_span":"Any person acquiring a foreclosed property containing one or more residential rental units must provide notices to the tenants in English and Spanish, within 10 business days after the sale","interaction":"Federal law does not preempt any State or local law that provides longer time periods or other additional protections for tenants in foreclosure proceedings.","relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Senior Citizens and Disabled Protected Tenancy Act","requirement":"Eligible senior, disabled and disabled-veteran tenants living in a building at least one year before a condominium, cooperative or fee simple conversion may be protected from eviction for up to 40 years, subject to a family income limit.","key_value":"up to 40 years; income limit 3x county average per-person income or $50,000.00, whichever is greater","coverage_conditions":"Rental buildings being converted to condominium, cooperative or fee simple ownership whose tenants meet the age, disability and one-year residency requirements.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Tenant is at least 62 before the conversion recording date, or permanently disabled, or a veteran disabled at 60% or more from service, and lived in the building at least one year before the conversion recording date.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.28","quoted_span":"Tenants may be protected from eviction for 40 years if their family income is not more than three (3) times the average per person income in their county","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Tenant Protection Act of 1992","requirement":"The Tenant Protection Act of 1992 extends protected-tenancy protections to qualified tenants in qualified counties, currently only Hudson County, in buildings converted or being converted who were not eligible under the Senior Citizens and Disabled Protected Tenancy Act of 1981.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Buildings converted or being converted in a qualified county; currently the only qualified county is Hudson County.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"other","role":"covered","text":"Buildings converted or being converted in qualified counties; currently only Hudson County"}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["At the present time, the only qualified county is Hudson County (N.J.A.C. 5:24-3.2(b))."]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.40","quoted_span":"At the present time, the only qualified county is Hudson County (N.J.A.C. 5:24-3.2(b)).","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","n_rules":8,"note":null}

